/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  column09_tray_hydraulics -- post-processing chain: ONE UNIT, FIVE ITEMS.

  This is the first case in the corpus where a single flowsheet unit is sized
  as several physical objects.  A `distillationColumn` is one MATHEMATICAL
  operation and, on the ground, five things somebody buys:

      shell        the tower                    costed as a vertical vessel
      trays        the tray stack               NOT COSTED -- see below
      condenser    a shell-and-tube exchanger
      reboiler     a shell-and-tube exchanger
      refluxDrum   a drum for the condensate    costed as a vessel

  Run the case and open `design/column09/` -- one specification sheet per item,
  each with its inlets, its outlets, what was sized, the RULE that produced the
  size, and what it costs.

  WHERE THE DIAMETER COMES FROM.  Not from this file: it is the answer the
  `hydraulics {}` block in `system/flowsheetDict` already computed, and the
  sizing pass reads it off the column's own KPIs.  That is the whole point of
  the ORDER -- the trays have to be able to pass the traffic before there is a
  tower to cost.  The run also reports the two SECTION diameters: the
  rectifying trays need 1.21 m and the stripping trays 1.32 m, which is 8 %
  apart.  Below roughly 15-20 % the transition cone of a swaged tower costs
  more than the plate a narrower section saves, so the tower is built STRAIGHT
  at the larger diameter -- an ECONOMIC decision, not a thermodynamic one, and
  Choupo reports both numbers rather than pretending to price the transition.

  WHAT THIS FILE DECLARES, AND WHY IT MUST.  U, the approach temperature and
  the drum's residence time are NOT consequences of a converged column: they
  are choices about the SERVICE -- which coolant, which steam level, how much
  surge the operator wants -- and they are the author's.  The engine refuses
  the item by name rather than substituting a default U, because a default U
  would be priced into the capital cost as though somebody had chosen it.
  The values below are THIS CASE'S declaration and no curated datum:
    * condenser  U 500 W/m2/K, LMTD 48 K   -- organic vapour condensing against
      cooling water taken from 25 to 40 C, against a 81 C overhead.
    * reboiler   U 800 W/m2/K, LMTD 17 K   -- LP steam against a 110 C bottoms.
    * drum       5 minutes of condensate holdup, the usual operability figure.
  Change them and every area, weight and cost below changes with them.

  THE TRAY STACK IS SIZED AND NOT COSTED, AND THE RUN SAYS SO.  Choupo's
  costing model holds eight coefficient sets and every coefficient in it is
  Turton's; there is no tray set, and inventing one would turn "uncosted" into
  "falsely costed", which no reader could detect.  So the trays refuse by name,
  the totals line reads INCOMPLETE, and the capital cost of this column is its
  shell, its two exchangers and its drum -- missing exactly the trays.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

sizing
{
    units
    (
        {
            unitName    column09;
            type        distillationColumn;
            material    carbonSteel;
            designRules
            {
                //  The same spacing the unit's `hydraulics {}` block declares.
                //  It is what turns a stage COUNT into a tower HEIGHT.
                traySpacing     0.50;       // m
                pressureDesign  2.0;        // bar (atmospheric column, x2 margin)
                corrosionAllow  0.003;      // m
                jointEfficiency 1.0;

                //  The two end spaces are left UNDECLARED on purpose, so this
                //  case shows what an engine default looks like when it is
                //  announced: the run prints `[assumed] distillationColumn
                //  'column09': disengagementHeight ...` and the shell's sheet
                //  carries an `assumed ( ... )` line naming both.  Declare
                //  `disengagementHeight` and `sumpHeight` here to own them.

                condenser
                {
                    U               500.0;      // W/m2/K -- declared, see header
                    LMTD            48.0;       // K
                    pressureDesign  2.0;        // bar
                }

                reboiler
                {
                    U               800.0;      // W/m2/K -- declared, see header
                    LMTD            17.0;       // K
                    pressureDesign  2.0;        // bar
                }

                refluxDrum
                {
                    residenceTime   300.0;      // s -- 5 minutes of condensate
                    pressureDesign  2.0;        // bar
                    L_over_D        3.0;
                    corrosionAllow  0.003;      // m
                    jointEfficiency 1.0;
                }
            }
        }
    );
}

costing
{
    method      Turton;
    year        2026;
    cepci       820;        // target-year CEPCI
    cepci2001   397;        // Turton base-year basis
    usdToEur    0.92;
}
